>remove manacles
You tug at the manacles, and feel the Captain's hand firm on your wrist. "Now, now, don't fight with them," he mutters.

"Here," says the Captain, and all at once you are outside the Guardhouse. You are hassled through the door, through the marble-floored lobby and down stairs. Stairs lead down to more stairs, ever onward it seems, until you are thrust into a dark cell, in a line of dark cells. Your hands remain bound in manacles, and you stumble on the doorframe and fall heavily onto your chest. The door slams, and when you look up you notice immediately with fear that the darkness has gone.

Night falls as you wait.

Cell, Night
The bars of your cell form one wall, the remaining three are solid rock, broken only by the small barred window. There is no bed, there is no bucket. There is no escape, but for you there is hope. You sit and wait for that other direction to become available. Time takes a long time to pass as you wait.

